  "title": "run-epic writes nothing to stdout while it runs",
  "body": "Tick 55i's description names it as related: `ticfac run-epic` produces no stdout while a run is live, so a redirected log is not a monitoring signal and the event feed is the only one — which is what raised the cost of the three defects this tick fixed. A progress line per stage (or even a pointer to `ticfac events --follow <run-id>`) would give operators a second, zero-cost signal.",
